PIM Access Scheduling (PAS) 是IANUS提出的面向NPU-PIM统一内存系统的调度框架，解决PIM memory同时服务NPU normal memory access和PIM computation时的资源冲突和数据依赖问题。在统一内存系统中，同一PIM bank不能同时执行normal read/write和PIM compute——两者互斥。PAS包含三层调度：(1) Workload Mapping——基于analytical model在compile time决定每个FC操作映射到MU还是PIM；(2) Mapping-Aware Scheduling——为multi-head attention的QK^T和SV操作选择执行单元（PIM或MU）并排布流水线；(3) Memory Access Scheduling——运行时协调macro PIM command和DMA normal access的分时复用。

从kernel调度角度拆解术语，比如术语所在kernel调度的伪代码或具体计算过程，给出具体例子。通过联网搜索让回答具体和精准。
PAS的核心调度逻辑（以GPT-2 decoder的generation step为例）：

```
// Phase 1: Compile-time Workload Mapping (Algorithm 1 in IANUS)
for each cmd in ordered_commands:
    if cmd.type == MU_FC:
        // Analytical model for MU execution time
        prev_cmd = CMDs[i-1]
        if prev_cmd.type == VU:
            t_prefetch = VU_model(n, prev_cmd.dim)  // weight prefetch overlap with VU
        w_cfg = cmd.weight_config
        w_load = DMA_weight(w_cfg.row, T)           // DMA weight loading time per tile
        mu_tile = MU_FC(n, w_cfg.row, T)            // MU compute time per tile
        mu_unpipe = mu_tile + w_load                 // First tile: load + compute
        mu_pipe = (w_cfg.col / T) * max(w_load, mu_tile)  // Pipeline: overlap load+compute
        mu_total = mu_unpipe + mu_pipe - t_prefetch  // Total MU time with prefetch

        pim_time = n * PIM_model(w_cfg.row, w_cfg.col)  // PIM: n tokens × per-token time

        if pim_time < mu_total:
            cmd.type = PIM  // Offload FC to PIM
            if cmd is first_FC_of_FFN:
                next_GELU_cmd.type = PIM  // Chain GELU to PIM (hardware support)

// Phase 2: Mapping-Aware Scheduling for Multi-Head Attention
// Summarization stage: FC_Q/K/V → MU, QK^T/SV → based on workload
// Schedule: generate K first → key transposition (DMA-based) parallel with V generation
// Utilize intra-head parallel (multiple heads simultaneously) + inter-head pipeline
for each head i in [0, h-1]:
    MU: W_Q^i @ x → Q_i     // Head i Q projection
    MU: W_K^i @ x → K_i     // Head i K projection  
    DMA: K_i transposition   // On-chip via AM→WM DMA + streaming buffer
    MU: W_V^i @ x → V_i     // Head i V projection (overlaps with K transposition)
MU/PIM: Q_i @ K_i^T → S_i  // Attention scores (parallel with next head's Q/K/V)
VU: softmax(S_i)             // With 1-bit bitmap masking
PIM/MU: S_i @ V_i → Z_i     // Weighted sum
VU: W_O @ concat(Z_0..Z_h-1) → attention_output  // Output projection (MU) + residual (VU)

// Phase 3: Runtime Memory Access Scheduling
scheduler:
    when macro_PIM_cmd becomes ready:
        // Block normal DMA to off-chip memory
        for each unissued DMA_cmd targeting off-chip memory:
            DMA_cmd.state = WAIT
        // Issue macro PIM command to PCU
        PCU.issue(macro_PIM_cmd)

    PCU:
        micro_cmds = decode(macro_PIM_cmd)  // One FC → 128 banks × multi-row micro cmds
        for each micro_cmd in micro_cmds:
            NoC.broadcast(micro_cmd, target_channels)
        wait_all_completions()
        signal_completion_to_scheduler()

    scheduler:
        on_PIM_completion():
            // Release blocked DMA commands
            for each waiting DMA_cmd:
                DMA_cmd.state = READY
```

从kernel调度角度，PAS的关键权衡在Algorithm 1中体现：当input tokens少时（如generation, n=1），PIM顺序处理每个token，但MU需通过128 token tile size column-tiling并等待weight loading——此时PIM更快（无需weight从PIM memory加载到scratch-pad的额外延迟）；当input tokens多时（如summarization, n=512），MU利用systolic array的128-wide parallelism + weight loading pipelining优势——MU更快。Algorithm 1在4-16 input tokens范围内达94%准确率选择最优unit。

